# atomic sandbox replay v1
# M5 "Drag far -> fallback lights up, the model learns" and fix rounds 3-4 "once it falls back it
# comes back" (re-check by hand: drag H2 far apart while playing, then let go): the estimated
# solver samples H2 (the automatic pass, about 40 s) and plays on the model; with nucleus 1 pinned
# (so the pull stretches the bond instead of towing the molecule) a Select-drag pulls nucleus 0
# out toward 3.34 Bohr from nucleus 1 and holds it there for 1.5 s; the wheel during the drag
# raises the pull from 0.1 to 0.305 Ha/Bohr (x1.25 per notch, UI checklist "drag pull"). Out there
# the model is unsure and DFT answers (fallbacks, each kept as a sample); after the release and
# the unpin the bond swings back, and 400 steps later the model answers again. How many fallbacks
# the drag causes depends on the machine (wall-paced input against a 16 ms tick); stderr names them.
view 1400 900
action smooth-motion false
action preset h2
wait idle
action backend estimated
wait idle
action tool select
t 100 cursor 0.1043005 0.0244677
action play
wait steps 20
action pin 1 true
t 200 button left down
t 210 wheel 5
t 240 cursor 0.1543005 0.0244677
wait ms 50
t 290 cursor 0.2043005 0.0244677
wait ms 50
t 340 cursor 0.2543005 0.0244677
wait ms 50
t 390 cursor 0.3043005 0.0244677
wait ms 50
t 440 cursor 0.3543005 0.0244677
wait ms 50
t 490 cursor 0.4043005 0.0244677
wait ms 1500
t 1990 button left up
action pin 1 false
wait steps 400
expect source surrogate
action pause
wait idle
expect no-error
